# the first read of the variable makes the RegExp and stores it, which no row and no look at a loop says: in front of the loop the read would hand the mark to every turn, and each turn would make a RegExp of its own
# const pattern = /a+/;  function same(n) { .. for (..) { const now = pattern; .. } }
# the loop calls nothing and stores nothing, so a plain read of a variable would be built in front of it
# with Guesses the loop is built twice for the sake of the dead zone of `pattern`, and in front of it the read is built WITH the test for the mark and the making: walk/loops/object-that-its-first-read-makes-is-made-in-front-of-a-loop.ir
